This project is a Polish adaptation of PingPong (Ilya Gusev, "PingPong: A Benchmark for Role-Playing Language Models
with User Emulation and Multi-Model Evaluation", arXiv:2409.06820, https://github.com/IlyaGusev/ping_pong_bench),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Taken from PingPong and changed:
- The method: an interrogator model emulates the user according to a hidden situation, the player model answers in
  character, judge models rate every player turn on three criteria (in character, entertaining, fluent; Likert 1-5),
  and the final score is the mean of the three criteria.
- Seven v2 situations, translated into Polish (anti_turing, environment, fight, rude, bio, typical_user, date).
  The undress_light situation was replaced by "targ" (bargaining with an NPC).
- The judge criteria, translated into Polish, with notes on Polish grammar, dialects and archaic language.
- The interrogator prompt, translated into Polish.

New in PingPong-PL (not from PingPong):
- Eight original Polish characters (data/characters.json); none comes from the original dataset.
- All code in this repository (run.py, make_packets.py, judge_codex.py, score.py), written from scratch.
- Two-judge blind rounds with anonymised packets, bootstrap intervals and paired sign tests.
